medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-06","finding":"Written Feeding Instructions - Signed and Dated by Parent or Health-Care Professional: Information obtained during investigation; determined the same infant was not served their last PM bottle on two separate occasions.","topic":"food","source_record_id":"1026576197","violation_type_title":"Written Feeding Instructions - Signed and Dated by Parent or Health-Care Professional (26 TAC §746.2421(a))","topic_label":"Food & nutrition"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1171242-i20240716-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-305-a-6","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1171242-i20240716","date":"2024-07-16","original_code":"746.305(a)(6)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-06","finding":"Report Situation Placing Children at Risk: Based on the information collected for this investigation, it was learned that the operation did not notify licensing when the staff failed to feed an infant their breast milk bottle on two separate occasions.   It was discovered that one of the incidents, due to the lack of proper labeling of bottles, uncovered the infant caregiver served an infant the wrong breast milk bottle. Both caregivers in the classroom were aware of the situation and did not informed the director. Therefore, the operation did not notify licensing.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026576198","violation_type_title":"Report Situation Placing Children at Risk (26 TAC §746.305(a)(6))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1171242-i20240612","date":"2024-06-12","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905806631","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905806631","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.7